cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent Harness Bench: an evidence-first coding-agent benchmark"
message: "If you use this benchmark, its data or its figures, please cite this repository."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ddawnlll/agent-harness-bench"
url: "https://github.com/ddawnlll/agent-harness-bench"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible comparison of three coding agents (Pi-Bolt, JCode, Hax) on
  three engineering tasks under an identical provider, model and reasoning
  effort. Nine trials, independent hidden graders, cgroup v2 resource
  accounting, provider-reported token usage and a single-file forensic audit.
  One trial per agent-task: the result is a screening signal, not a universal
  ranking.
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - safety
  - reproducibility
authors:
  - name: ddawnlll
